  "Question": "What is the constant term in the expansion of \\((x+1)^6\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "1",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The constant term contains no \\(x\\), meaning the exponent of \\(x\\) is 0. Its coefficient is \\(C(6,6)=1\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Evaluate at zero\n\nThe constant term is the only term of a polynomial that remains when \\(x=0\\), since all positive powers of \\(x\\) vanish. Therefore the constant term of \\((x+1)^6\\) is\n\\[\n(0+1)^6=1.\n\\]",
